import csv,json,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
CASES={
'199903432':('REFUTED','The s56 P and P/2 predictions follow a smooth downward SAP drift; the P window at 2837.59 has 185 core cadences but only one right-side baseline cadence. A second P/2 minimum near 2852.29 follows another drift. At the P prediction in s83, 3571.78, 86 core cadences and 223/238 side cadences yield 0.0 ppt. This is contrary to a repeated 7 ppt eclipse at the fold period.','Fold minima are on evolving s56 baselines; no credible measured eclipse center or depth.','Revisit only if an independently observed, stable-baseline dip is found.'),
'423569223':('PLAUSIBLE','The s101 event around BTJD 4119 has a broad depression and recovery toward an observing gap. Its center and complete profile are uncertain; the target-centered cutout also shows aperture-dependent drifts at other times in the sector. The P prediction in s63 is nearly flat, but the pre-center portion includes a gap, so it is not treated as a decisive full null. The folded search does not establish a repeated eclipse clock.','One possible event, no measured same-kind repeat, ambiguous cycle count and source attribution.','Obtain a continuous future event and difference-pixel localization; then test integer-cycle aliases.'),
'393487481':('REFUTED','Raw s45/s46 light curves show repeated non-detached waves and evolving baselines. The s46 P/2 feature near 2567 is a partial recovery just after an orbit gap, resembling another post-gap ramp near 2553. The s72 broad depression near 3270 occurs within multiday drift and abrupt level changes. Neither is a stable detached-eclipse profile.','The aperture varies, but instrumental ramps and real stellar variability are not separated; the 28.79/14.35 d selected fold signal is refuted as evidence for eclipses.','Characterize variability with independent photometry before revisiting any eclipse hypothesis.'),
'250225622':('REFUTED','The s55 prediction falls at a segment boundary with no left-side baseline. In s82, a roughly 9% level jump around BTJD 3545.4 precedes the predicted 3546.01 window; the flux then recovers smoothly. In s92, the 3804.05 P prediction falls on a long rising ramp, and the P/2 prediction 3822.48 falls on a separate decline and later step. These are changing segment baselines rather than repeating isolated eclipses.','Large sector-scale instrumental or extraction trends prevent a physical depth or center from being measured.','Use a stable independent light curve if a new isolated event appears.'),
'247563559':('REFUTED','P predictions at 2519.67 (s44) and 3282.69 (s72) are flat within about 0.4 ppt with complete nearby side coverage. The apparent -5.9 ppt s98 core at 3994.85 lies on a broad multi-day ramp with abrupt changes around 3990 and 4008. The same-kind 50.87 d fold recurrence is contradicted by the earlier covered windows.','The s98 baseline is unstable; this refutes the selected fold eclipse interpretation, not every possible shorter-period signal.','Inspect a future stable-window event if one emerges.'),
'23885936':('REFUTED','In s51, SAP drops about 20 ppt abruptly near BTJD 2716 and remains low to the end of that observing segment; this is a step, not a completed eclipse. KSPSAP changes by only about 6 ppt in the same selected core. The next P prediction in s91 at 3795.68 has 103 core and 237/233 side cadences, yielding +0.2 ppt rather than the fold 6.5 ppt dip.','The s51 step and pipeline-dependent amplitude invalidate a measured eclipse clock.','Check a new stable-baseline dip if available.'),
'41859748':('REFUTED','The s104 proposed depression lies between large level changes near 4185 and 4198; the P prediction at 4197.36 samples the recovery side of that low plateau. The s69 P prediction 3201.25 has 196 core and 237/238 side cadences with only -0.4 ppt versus the fold 1.15 ppt depth, useful context but not a calibrated sensitive null. The s104 step pattern drives the fold peak.','Later s105–107 cutouts are exploratory coverage; they are not asserted as sensitivity-calibrated nulls. A different subtle event remains possible.','Seek a complete, independently timed event with stable background.'),
'295743311':('REFUTED','The s87 P prediction 3688.61 is on a broad ramp in SAP. A WCS-centered TESSCut check gives +2.65 ppt in the smaller aperture and -0.21 ppt in the larger aperture, inconsistent with a stable 3.41 ppt eclipse. Newly available s108 covers the P prediction 4314.445 with 138 quality-0 core cadences and 0.60/0.11 ppt in those apertures. Its repeated ramps and jumps show the same extraction behavior away from the proposed period.','Aperture scale strongly changes the apparent feature; no measured eclipse center. The two extractions share photons.','Follow up only a new isolated event with difference-image attribution.'),
'339095955':('REFUTED','The s73 3288.88 P/P2 prediction lies in the sector-start recovery and adjacent level step; it is a rising trend rather than a detached 12.8 ppt eclipse. The s19 prediction near 1830.68 has one-sided coverage and structured variability. The s59 prediction lies in a gap. There is no second reliable same-kind event at either 28.04 or 14.03 d.','The apparent fold depth is dominated by an evolving baseline and gaps; no photometric period is measured.','Test any future isolated dip on a continuous baseline.'),
'452298854':('REFUTED','At P=54.733 d the s41 prediction 2425.72 is flat with 35 core and 79/63 side cadences (-0.3 ppt); s75 near 3356.18 has only a noisy -2.0 ppt fluctuation compared with the 6.57 ppt folded depth, and s81 has sparse core coverage. The s14 and s54 P/2 windows show similarly small changes within broader fluctuating light curves. These covered inconsistencies contradict a coherent folded eclipse.','Several apparent fluctuations are weak and source attribution is not established; this verdict addresses the selected fold claim.','Reassess if future data yield a coherent detached event.'),
}
rows=[]
for q in csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf-8')):
 tic=q['tic'];verdict,reason,limits,next_check=CASES[tic];d=B/tic
 ins=json.loads((d/'fold-inspection.json').read_text());src=json.loads((B.parent/'source-packets'/tic/'sources.json').read_text());avail=json.loads((B/'sector-availability.json').read_text())[tic]
 fs=', '.join(f"s{f['sector']} BTJD {f['start']:.2f}–{f['end']:.2f} ({f['n']} quality-0 SAP cadences)" for f in ins['files'])
 trials=', '.join(f"{k}={ins['fold_trials'][k]['P']:.5f} d, predicted depth {ins['fold_trials'][k]['depth']/1000:.2f} ppt" for k in ('P','P2'))
 add=''
 if tic=='295743311':add=' The [current-sector aperture check](cutout-check.json) records target WCS positions, exact core/side counts, and source cutout hashes.'
 if tic in ('423569223','393487481','41859748'):add=' The independent [helper pixel audit](../helper-audit.md) checks target WCS apertures. Gaia neighbor cone queries returned 503, so capable neighbors are not excluded.'
 report=f"# {q['sample_id']} — TIC {tic}\n\n**Physical verdict: {verdict}. Bounded review: COMPLETE. Catalogue novelty: UNKNOWN.** This is one frozen period_fold_only lead, not a new counted acceptance.\n\n{reason}\n\nThe search tried {trials}; Gaia SB1 orbital P={float(q['gaia_period_days']):.5f} d is separate spectroscopy, not a measured eclipse period. No reliable photometric period, timing epoch, error, or physical depth is assigned. P and P/2 predicted occasions and quality-filtered raw measurements are in [fold-inspection.json](fold-inspection.json) and [the event panels](fold-predicted-windows.png). Coverage: {fs}. The [full-sector plots](orbit-context.png) and [Gaia geometry estimates](orbit-context.json) provide context; conjunction predictions assume an edge-on orbit and do not establish eclipse timing. TESSCut currently lists {', '.join(map(str,avail.get('available_sectors',[])))}; unobserved or uncached windows are not called nulls.{add}\n\n**Limits and next check.** {limits} {next_check} A single reduction of TESS photons does not supply an independent observing occasion. The four central catalogue novelty gates remain unavailable, so UNKNOWN does not mean novel. [Source hashes](source-hashes.json) verify the packet, original bulk/fold results, and every used QLP FITS; the cutout receipts preserve any additional bytes.\n"
 rp=d/'REPORT.md';rp.write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
 rows.append({'sample_id':q['sample_id'],'tic':tic,'sample_stratum':q['sample_stratum'],'physical_verdict':verdict,'full_review_completion':'COMPLETE','novelty_status':'UNKNOWN','period_days':'','period_error_days':'','primary_epoch_btjd':'','depth_ppt':'','limitations':limits,'next_check':next_check,'report':str(rp)})
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(rows[0]));w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print([(r['sample_id'],r['physical_verdict']) for r in rows])
